<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Profurn raises interim shr, no div.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Profurn raises interim shr, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  4.6	   vs 2.4</p>
<p>    Net income		25.38	 vs 11.42</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   38.07	 vs 16.22</p>
<p>    Tax			 12.69	 vs 4.80</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   1.91	  vs 0.95</p>
<p>    Turnover		  332.79	vs 174.57</p>
<p>Full name: Protea Furnishers Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that its dividend policy remained to declare only a final dividend at the end of each year which will be covered not less than three times.</p>
<p>Profurn said that it planned to open a further 25 stores before year end of which 12 will be in South Africa and 13 in the neighbouring states. The group's first store in Mozambique will be opened in August. It said preparations are at an advanced stage in Kenya, Uganda and Tanzania where trading will commence during the course of 1998.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
